twox-hash

Portions of the XXH3 SIMD kernels are adapted from twox-hash 2.1.4. Each local
path is followed by its upstream source paths:

  src/xxhash/kernel/neon.rs
    src/xxhash3/large/neon.rs
  src/xxhash/kernel/x86.rs
    src/xxhash3/large/sse2.rs
    src/xxhash3/large/avx2.rs

The fixed upstream revision is:

  https://github.com/shepmaster/twox-hash/tree/6f866bffe73900c63df2650be4eed41e3ed9b500

The NEON adaptation includes four-lane accumulation, the scheduling barrier,
and 64-by-32-bit multiplication. The x86 adaptation covers stripe
accumulation; scrambling follows xxHash's SIMD routines. Hashcrew uses its
own kernel interface and backend selection.

